Common-size statements scale items by a shared base, usually sales or assets.|₹20 expense on ₹100 sales is 20%.|₹30 expense on ₹150 sales is…?|20%|30%|50%
Horizontal analysis compares periods; vertical analysis compares components within one statement.|Sales rise ₹100 to ₹120, a 20% increase.|Expressing rent as a share of sales is…?|Vertical analysis|Horizontal growth|Debt valuation
Growth and trend analysis separates rate, persistence, and drivers.|Sales ₹100 to ₹110 grow 10%; ₹110 to ₹121 also grow 10%.|Constant percentage growth implies constant absolute increases?|No|Yes|Only annually
Liquidity ratios assess short-term coverage; current and quick ratios use different asset perimeters.|Current assets ₹100 and liabilities ₹50 give current ratio 2.|Does ratio 2 guarantee timely cash payment?|No|Yes|Only for audited firms
Profit margins relate defined earnings to sales; each subtotal captures different costs.|Net profit ₹10 on sales ₹100 gives 10% net margin.|₹15 net profit on ₹150 sales gives…?|10%|15%|90%
Turnover measures sales or costs relative to average operating assets.|Sales ₹200 and average assets ₹100 give asset turnover 2.|Higher turnover automatically means higher profit?|No|Yes|Only in retail
Leverage measures debt exposure; coverage measures ability to meet financing charges.|EBIT ₹30 and interest ₹5 give interest coverage 6.|Interest coverage here is…?|6 times|25 times|0.17 times
ROA, ROE, ROCE, and ROIC use different profits and capital bases; match numerator and denominator.|NOPAT ₹12 on average invested capital ₹100 gives ROIC 12%.|Should ROIC normally include debt interest in its operating numerator?|No|Yes|Only when debt exists
DuPont decomposes ROE into margin, turnover, and financial leverage.|10% margin × 2 turnover × 1.5 equity multiplier gives 30% ROE.|A higher multiplier can raise ROE while raising…?|Financial risk|Cash sales necessarily|Product quality
Cash conversion compares earnings with operating cash; cash-cycle analysis traces operating balances.|Profit ₹20 and CFO ₹12 give CFO/profit 60%.|Low conversion necessarily proves fraud?|No|Yes|Only for growing firms
Operating leverage comes from fixed operating costs; financial leverage from financing obligations.|Revenue ₹100, variable costs ₹60, fixed costs ₹30 leave EBIT ₹10.|A 10% sales rise at unchanged prices and costs raises EBIT to…?|₹14|₹11|₹20
Sustainable growth considers retained earnings and stable leverage; internal growth excludes external financing.|Under a simplified steady-state relation, 15% ROE × 60% retention gives 9% sustainable growth.|Growth financed by borrowing alone is internal growth?|No|Yes|Only for profitable firms
Incremental return measures additional operating profit relative to additional invested capital.|ΔNOPAT ₹3 over Δcapital ₹20 gives 15% incremental return.|With required return 10%, this increment appears…?|Value creating under assumptions|Value destroying|Unrelated to value
Segment analysis separates differing business economics and central costs.|Retail margin 5% and software margin 30% make a blended margin mix-sensitive.|A blended improvement necessarily means both segments improved?|No|Yes|Only with stable revenue
Peer benchmarking requires comparable business models, policies, and industry metrics.|A bank's net interest margin and a retailer's gross margin answer different questions.|Should they be compared as identical margins?|No|Yes|Only in one currency
Normalisation removes justified non-recurring distortions and restores sustainable economics.|Reported profit ₹20 includes ₹5 disposal gain: simplified normalised profit ₹15.|Every management exclusion should be accepted?|No|Yes|Only if labelled exceptional
Seasonality repeats within years; cyclicality spans business cycles; base effects distort growth percentages.|Sales rebound ₹50 to ₹100 after a depressed period: 100% growth.|Does that rate prove long-run 100% growth?|No|Yes|Only for listed companies
Reported, adjusted, and underlying measures require transparent bridges and consistent definitions.|Reported profit ₹20 + excluded expense ₹3 gives adjusted ₹23.|What must accompany the adjusted number?|A justified reconciliation|Only management confidence|Only a new label
